 "method": {
  "rule": "A column is a hidden FK if its NAME ends in 'ID', its TYPE is not a typed object reference (does not end in ' ID'), its type is not a code-table 'Dropdown (...)', and the name minus the 'ID' suffix matches a real object in the 227.",
  "exclusion": "150 rows were excluded as the table's OWN primary key (e.g. Contract.ContractID typed Number). A PK is not an FK and counting it would have inflated the result from 87 to 237. This was the first cut and it was wrong."
 },
